    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.the-same-totem-animal-at-the": "The same totem naaldlooshii at the same pillar — éí doodago the same naaldlooshii in a different \"ring\" born 12, 24, éí doodago 36 years apart. Same naʼnitiní; wonderfully different diné.",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.totem-connections": "<a href=\"connections.html?v=20260807\">← Totem Connections</a>",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.the-same-totem-animal-at-the.2": "The same totem naaldlooshii at the same level — someone who shares ní Spirit, Mind, Heart, éí doodago Body naʼnitiní exactly. It can also be diné bitsʼą́ą́dę́ę́ʼ different 'rings' so to speak — in other words diné born 12, 24, 36, éí doodago some other multiple of 12 years apart bitsʼą́ą́dę́ę́ʼ you. For example, I am a Fire Tiger born in 1986, but I have some wonderful Tiger hooghan dóó friends who are born in different Tiger rings — one of my uncles is a Water Tiger born in 1962, my son is a Metal Tiger born in 2010, dóó several dear friends, students, dóó companions are Earth Tigers born in 1998. I've also had coworkers who were born in the nááhai of the Wood Tiger, 1974. It can be cool to see how ní naaldlooshii act when they've got different elemental flavors charging their energy in other diné. It can also be neat to find diné born on the same exact birthdate as you, so they've got all the same naaldlooshii naʼnitiní, éí doodago at least 3 out of 4 if the hour naaldlooshii is different, dóó to see how they've chosen to play their hand differently than the way you've chosen to play yours — kind of like how 'identical' twins are different in many respects, but share lots of things in other areas. Free will is a powerful thing, dóó díí connection shows éí most clearly. The birth naaldlooshii guiding them are the same, but the diné being guided still turn out completely dóó wonderfully different :)",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.h3.other-connection-types": "Other connection types",
