    "article.nepalTime.p.from-the-jade-emperor-atop-the": "Manta the Jade Emperor atop the Kun Lun mountains to the Buddha’s birthplace in Nepal — why ñoqanchik convert to NPT before qampa uywakuna are drawn.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.how-it-works": "<a href=\"how-it-works.html\">← Imayna Llamkan</a>",
    "article.nepalTime.p.before-your-animals-are-calculated-we": "Before qampa uywakuna are calculated, ñoqanchik convert qampa birth moment to <strong>Nepal Time (NPT, UTC+5:45)</strong> — a timezone shift rooted in an intuitive discovery chay kay so-called “Chinese Astrology” system actually has its roots in myths about the Jade Emperor, who dwelt atop the Jade Mountain in the K’un Lun Mountain Range serving as Tibet’s northern border. It then gets delivered down to us humans manta the Buddha, whose birthplace is traditionally held to be in Nepal. Thus converting birth times to NPT first helps the pʼunchaw hinaspa hour uywakuna line up wan the truths runakuna all over the pacha recognize in their own Hearts hinaspa Bodies.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.in-myths-the-jade-emperor-dwelt": "In myths, the Jade Emperor dwelt in the Jade Castle of Abstraction, high above the earth hinaspa the thirty-kimsa heavens, according to some accounts; utaq according to others, on the Mountain of Jade in the K’un Lun range. Here, on the shore of the Jade Lake, grew a Jade Tree, which measured kimsa hundred arm lengths across hinaspa whose red jade fruit conferred the boon of eternal life.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.if-you-enter-your-birth-time": "If you enter qampa paqariy hora as recorded on qampa birth certificate — say, 3:15 PM in Denver utaq 9:00 AM in London — the calculator first honors chay local time exactly. Then, before any pillar is calculated, it converts chay moment to Nepal Time hinaspa uses chay shifted time for qampa totem pole.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.on-the-calculator-results-you-will": "On the calculator results, you will always see both times side by side: the time you entered, qampa paqariy llaqta’s timezone, hinaspa the equivalent <strong>Nepal Time (NPT)</strong> used for the actual calculation. If you were born in Kathmandu, the shift may show no change — but for most births worldwide, the conversion matters.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.read-more-of-the-personal-story": "Astawan ñawinchay of the personal story behind kay discovery on the <a href=\"about.html\">About</a> page.",
    "article.nepalTime.h2.see-both-times-on-your-totem": "Iskay Horakunata Totem Pole-niykipi Qhawariy",
    "article.nepalTime.p.the-calculator-shows-your-local-birth": "The calculator shows qampa local paqariy hora hinaspa the Nepal Time used for qampa pillars.",
