    "article.sacredRoles.p.seeker-mage-and-royal-three-distinct": "Seeker, Mage, hinaspa Royal — kimsa distinct ways every Values Triangle uywa relates to its core value.",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.the-same-archetypal-structure-repeats-in": "The same archetypal structure repeats in every Values Triangle. Each triangle is a group of kimsa uywakuna chay includes one Seeker, one Mage, hinaspa one Royal — kimsa distinct ways of relating to chay Triangle's Core Value. Each uywa embodies their Core Value like a banner, just preferring to access it wan their own unique perspective.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-seeker-in-every-triangle-the": "<strong>The Seeker</strong> — In every triangle the Seeker is the one who pursues, acquires, hinaspa accumulates the Core Value, drawn to gather more of it utaq build it up themselves depending on their proclivities. For example, the Power hinaspa Harmony Seekers always seem to be in hot pursuit of their Core Value, chasing after it while the Seekers of Idealism hinaspa Security take a more active role in building their Core Value up directly, starting manta where they're at. The Security Seeker sets to work placing the blocks of the Pyramid one after the other, hinaspa Idealism insists upon Freedom at every turn wan a pure passion chay dares somebody to stop utaq even try to slow it down. They are the Drivers of each pack, ensuring chay things get done hinaspa empires get built, pushing for the team to get looked after hinaspa making sure everyone has somewhere to rest at the end of night.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-mage-each-mage-in-their": "<strong>The Mage</strong> — Each Mage in their triangle understands their Core Value so intuitively chay it becomes almost a plaything. Thus they are happy to work behind the scenes, wielding their Core Value subtly hinaspa deploying their strength in it wan strategic intelligence. It's more of a game to them than the deadly seriousness wan which the other two Roles treat their Core Values. At times the Mages might mana even appear to be in possession of their Core Value at all, but kay is just a surface-level appearance - they can access it wan lightning quickness at any time. The Mages are as committed to their goals as anybody, they're just going to have a good time dancing across the boundaries hinaspa testing the limits all along the way. Playfulness is part the package, but they've got an excellent hamutʼay of their Core Value whenever it truly counts.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-royal-these-four-animals-embody": "<strong>The Royal</strong> — These tawa uywa embody their Core Value at the center of their very Being, serving as Role Models of them hinaspa wielding chay Core Value wan a natural air of authority. Because of kay, others will follow their lead, so Spiderman rules apply: wan great power comes great responsibility! Royals often assume they have priority, hinaspa kay assumption works wonders in getting them a pass straight to the front of the line hinaspa directly to the center of the stage. The trick is in understating chay it's mana just a privilege to be out here in front; it's also hard work! The runakuna are directly counting on you for direction, so chay sense of knowing just what to do next better come in handy mana only for you but also for all those watching you to see how things get done. The Royals are born leaders who make the best use of the spotlight for showcasing what's important.",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.what-follows-on-the-values-triangles": "What follows on the <a href=\"totem-astrology.html\">Values Triangles</a> page is the canon for each triangle: the kimsa uywakuna hinaspa how each one lives its role as Seeker, Mage, utaq Royal.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.section-label.the-four-royals": "Tawa Royals",
