    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.of-the-twelve-totem-animals-four": "Of the chunka iskayniyuq totem uywakuna, tawa carry the Sacred Role of Royal — one in each Values Triangle. Together they form a double sovereignty over the zodiac: the <strong>Dragon</strong> hinaspa <strong>Phoenix</strong> as King hinaspa Queen of the <strong>Celestial Realm</strong>, hinaspa the <strong>Tiger</strong> hinaspa <strong>Bear</strong> as King hinaspa Queen of the <strong>Earthly Realm</strong>.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h3.the-celestial-realm": "Celestial Realm",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.the-dragon-and-phoenix-reign-over": "The Dragon hinaspa Phoenix reign over the realm of ideas hinaspa ethereal thought structures — templates, proclamations, standards, hinaspa the architecture of how things ought to be held in mind before they are lived in the body. The Dragon guards power hinaspa the templates of excellence; the Phoenix proclaims security through beauty, display, hinaspa the visible promise chay all is well.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h3.the-earthly-realm": "Earthly Realm",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.the-tiger-and-bear-reign-over": "The Tiger hinaspa Bear reign over the realm of instincts hinaspa juicy, sensuous experience — conviction felt in the chest, abundance tasted at the table, ideals embodied in motion, hinaspa harmony curated in the flesh of daily life. The Tiger radiates inspiration as living proof; the Bear, as Royal of Harmony, is guardian hinaspa protector of peace, holding the atmosphere others settle into through generosity, refuge, hinaspa unhurried authority.",
