    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.the-same-totem-animal-at-the": "The same totem uywa at the same pillar — utaq the same uywa in a different \"ring\" born 12, 24, utaq 36 years apart. Same guía-kuna; wonderfully different runakuna.",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.totem-connections": "<a href=\"connections.html?v=20260807\">← Totem Connections</a>",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.the-same-totem-animal-at-the.2": "The same totem uywa at the same level — someone who shares qampa Spirit, Mind, Heart, utaq Body guía exactly. It can also be runakuna manta different 'rings' so to speak — in other words runakuna born 12, 24, 36, utaq some other multiple of 12 years apart manta you. For example, I am a Fire Tiger born in 1986, but I have some wonderful Tiger ayllu hinaspa friends who are born in different Tiger rings — one of my uncles is a Water Tiger born in 1962, my son is a Metal Tiger born in 2010, hinaspa several dear friends, students, hinaspa companions are Earth Tigers born in 1998. I've also had coworkers who were born in the wata of the Wood Tiger, 1974. It can be cool to see how qampa uywakuna act when they've got different elemental flavors charging their energy in other runakuna. It can also be neat to find runakuna born on the same exact birthdate as you, so they've got all the same uywa guía-kuna, utaq at least 3 out of 4 if the hour uywa is different, hinaspa to see how they've chosen to play their hand differently than the way you've chosen to play yours — kind of like how 'identical' twins are different in many respects, but share lots of things in other areas. Free will is a powerful thing, hinaspa kay connection shows chay most clearly. The birth uywakuna guiding them are the same, but the runakuna being guided still turn out completely hinaspa wonderfully different :)",
