    "article.nepalTime.p.from-the-jade-emperor-atop-the": "Ta the Jade Emperor atop the Kun Lun mountains to the Buddha’s birthplace in Nepal — why jiwasa convert to NPT before juma uywanaka are drawn.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.how-it-works": "<a href=\"how-it-works.html\">← Kamisaki Lurasi</a>",
    "article.nepalTime.p.before-your-animals-are-calculated-we": "Before juma uywanaka are calculated, jiwasa convert juma birth moment to <strong>Nepal Time (NPT, UTC+5:45)</strong> — a timezone shift rooted in an intuitive discovery uka aka so-called “Chinese Astrology” system actually has its roots in myths about the Jade Emperor, who dwelt atop the Jade Mountain in the K’un Lun Mountain Range serving as Tibet’s northern border. It then gets delivered down to us humans ta the Buddha, whose birthplace is traditionally held to be in Nepal. Thus converting birth times to NPT first helps the uru ukat hour uywanaka line up mpi the truths jaqinaka all over the aka pacha recognize in their own Hearts ukat Bodies.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.in-myths-the-jade-emperor-dwelt": "In myths, the Jade Emperor dwelt in the Jade Castle of Abstraction, high above the earth ukat the thirty-kimsa heavens, according to some accounts; jan ukaxa according to others, on the Mountain of Jade in the K’un Lun range. Here, on the shore of the Jade Lake, grew a Jade Tree, which measured kimsa hundred arm lengths across ukat whose red jade fruit conferred the boon of eternal life.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.if-you-enter-your-birth-time": "If you enter juma yuriñ hora as recorded on juma birth certificate — say, 3:15 PM in Denver jan ukaxa 9:00 AM in London — the calculator first honors uka local time exactly. Then, before any pillar is calculated, it converts uka moment to Nepal Time ukat uses uka shifted time for juma totem pole.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.on-the-calculator-results-you-will": "On the calculator results, you will always see both times side by side: the time you entered, juma yuriñ marka’s timezone, ukat the equivalent <strong>Nepal Time (NPT)</strong> used for the actual calculation. If you were born in Kathmandu, the shift may show no change — but for most births worldwide, the conversion matters.",
    "article.nepalTime.p.read-more-of-the-personal-story": "Jukʼampiw liytʼaña of the personal story behind aka discovery on the <a href=\"about.html\">About</a> page.",
    "article.nepalTime.h2.see-both-times-on-your-totem": "Paya Horanaka Totem Pole-mani Uñjaña",
    "article.nepalTime.p.the-calculator-shows-your-local-birth": "The calculator shows juma local yuriñ hora ukat the Nepal Time used for juma pillars.",
