    "article.sacredRoles.section-label.totem-astrology": "Totem Astrology",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.seeker-mage-and-royal-three-distinct": "Seeker, Mage, ukat Royal — kimsa distinct ways every Values Triangle uywa relates to its core value.",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.the-same-archetypal-structure-repeats-in": "The same archetypal structure repeats in every Values Triangle. Each triangle is a group of kimsa uywanaka uka includes one Seeker, one Mage, ukat one Royal — kimsa distinct ways of relating to uka Triangle's Core Value. Each uywa embodies their Core Value like a banner, just preferring to access it mpi their own unique perspective.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-seeker-in-every-triangle-the": "<strong>The Seeker</strong> — In every triangle the Seeker is the one who pursues, acquires, ukat accumulates the Core Value, drawn to gather more of it jan ukaxa build it up themselves depending on their proclivities. For example, the Power ukat Harmony Seekers always seem to be in hot pursuit of their Core Value, chasing after it while the Seekers of Idealism ukat Security take a more active role in building their Core Value up directly, starting ta where they're at. The Security Seeker sets to work placing the blocks of the Pyramid one after the other, ukat Idealism insists upon Freedom at every turn mpi a pure passion uka dares somebody to stop jan ukaxa even try to slow it down. They are the Drivers of each pack, ensuring uka things get done ukat empires get built, pushing for the team to get looked after ukat making sure everyone has somewhere to rest at the end of night.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-mage-each-mage-in-their": "<strong>The Mage</strong> — Each Mage in their triangle understands their Core Value so intuitively uka it becomes almost a plaything. Thus they are happy to work behind the scenes, wielding their Core Value subtly ukat deploying their strength in it mpi strategic intelligence. It's more of a game to them than the deadly seriousness mpi which the other two Roles treat their Core Values. At times the Mages might janiw even appear to be in possession of their Core Value at all, but aka is just a surface-level appearance - they can access it mpi lightning quickness at any time. The Mages are as committed to their goals as anybody, they're just going to have a good time dancing across the boundaries ukat testing the limits all along the way. Playfulness is part the package, but they've got an excellent amuytʼawi of their Core Value whenever it truly counts.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-royal-these-four-animals-embody": "<strong>The Royal</strong> — These pusi uywa embody their Core Value at the center of their very Being, serving as Role Models of them ukat wielding uka Core Value mpi a natural air of authority. Because of aka, others will follow their lead, so Spiderman rules apply: mpi great power comes great responsibility! Royals often assume they have priority, ukat aka assumption works wonders in getting them a pass straight to the front of the line ukat directly to the center of the stage. The trick is in understating uka it's janiw just a privilege to be out here in front; it's also hard work! The jaqinaka are directly counting on you for direction, so uka sense of knowing just what to do next better come in handy janiw only for you but also for all those watching you to see how things get done. The Royals are born leaders who make the best use of the spotlight for showcasing what's important.",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.what-follows-on-the-values-triangles": "What follows on the <a href=\"totem-astrology.html\">Values Triangles</a> page is the canon for each triangle: the kimsa uywanaka ukat how each one lives its role as Seeker, Mage, jan ukaxa Royal.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.section-label.the-four-royals": "Pusi Royals",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h2.celestial-earthly-realms": "Celestial & Earthly Realms",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.of-the-twelve-totem-animals-four": "Of the tunka payani totem uywanaka, pusi carry the Sacred Role of Royal — one in each Values Triangle. Together they form a double sovereignty over the zodiac: the <strong>Dragon</strong> ukat <strong>Phoenix</strong> as King ukat Queen of the <strong>Celestial Realm</strong>, ukat the <strong>Tiger</strong> ukat <strong>Bear</strong> as King ukat Queen of the <strong>Earthly Realm</strong>.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h3.the-celestial-realm": "Celestial Realm",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.the-dragon-and-phoenix-reign-over": "The Dragon ukat Phoenix reign over the realm of ideas ukat ethereal thought structures — templates, proclamations, standards, ukat the architecture of how things ought to be held in mind before they are lived in the body. The Dragon guards power ukat the templates of excellence; the Phoenix proclaims security through beauty, display, ukat the visible promise uka all is well.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h3.the-earthly-realm": "Earthly Realm",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.the-tiger-and-bear-reign-over": "The Tiger ukat Bear reign over the realm of instincts ukat juicy, sensuous experience — conviction felt in the chest, abundance tasted at the table, ideals embodied in motion, ukat harmony curated in the flesh of daily life. The Tiger radiates inspiration as living proof; the Bear, as Royal of Harmony, is guardian ukat protector of peace, holding the atmosphere others settle into through generosity, refuge, ukat unhurried authority.",
