    "page.about.p.from-the-four-pillars-of-destiny": "Chi ru the Four Pillars of Destiny to a Nepalese timezone — the story of how Totem Astrology finally clicked into place.",
    "page.about.h2.travis-barrett-leblanc": "Travis Barrett LeBlanc",
    "page.about.p.relationship-counselor-multi-system-astr": "Relationship Counselor, Multi-System Astrologer, ut Personal Creator of Totem Astrology",
    "page.about.p.i-developed-totem-astrology-over-the": "I developed Totem Astrology over the past few decades by traveling the ruuchichʼochʼ, talking to thousands of different poyanam, ut studying many different astrological systems. I found the precious foundation in the Chinese Four Pillars of Destiny tradition specifically — while others have used aʼin herramienta for calculating fortunes ut fates, my intuition told me li it actually has something more to teach us about the basis for qa inner makeup.",
    "page.about.p.my-first-clue-was-the-four": "My first clue was the kaahibʼ parts: the Junabʼ, Ikʼ, Qʼehal, ut Hour. These had to correspond to qa Spirit, Mind, Heart, ut Body! I did the calculations, but something was still off. The upper half of the information rang true chi the Junabʼ ut the Ikʼ, but the bottom half chi the Qʼehal ut the Hour didn't seem to line up as well chi the facts of the poyanam standing right in front of me. I fiddled chi it for years before a sudden intuition clued me in: the Four Pillars System claims its birthright chi ru the Jade Emperor, in some traditions handed straight down chi ru the Buddha himself.",
    "page.about.p.since-the-buddha-s-traditional-birthplac": "Since the Buddha's traditional birthplace is in Nepal, I decided to start shifting poyanam's birth times to the Nepalese time zone before adding their info to the Four Pillars Calculator — ut suddenly, voilà! Aʼin new birth data finally clicked everything into place. So now here on qa website, the <a href=\"calculator.html\">Totem Calculator</a> does all li for you: just plug in aa qʼehal xaqʼeex, time, ut place, ut the shift is already incorporated before aa kaahibʼ xul come out. Now what you see really does line up chi aa Spirit, Mind, Heart, ut Body!",
    "page.about.h3.philosophy": "Filosofía",
    "page.about.p.i-like-to-think-of-these": "I like to think of these kaahibʼ xul as the cards you were dealt at the beginning of aʼin life. They are built right in there chi ru the beginning for you to take advantage of, but they don't seal aa fate in the slightest. You've always got the opportunity to work on them ut refine them, o even disregard them completely ut bluff sometimes if you want to! But it certainly helps to know what you're playing chi since the game is already in motion.",
    "page.about.p.a-central-tenet-of-totem-astrology": "A central tenet of Totem Astrology is suyankil — suyankil for a better naw of aat pach, suyankil to better naw aa xjunil ut junkabʼaal poyanam, ut suyankil li there is someone, o someones, out there who are compatible chi you just the way you are. The kaahibʼ guía give us a kind of jun aatin: something abstract to symbolize what is going on for us internally, so qo can talk about qa diferencias without every conversation turning into a trial.",
    "page.about.p.this-is-not-an-excuse-for": "Aʼin is ma an excuse for ma us comportamiento, nor is it a reason to accept other poyanam's ma us comportamiento. It is a herramienta for naw each other ut giving each other some grace — grace born chi ru comprehension of qa diferencias ut appreciation of the different modes poyanam operate within. When qo see li a loved one's tardiness might come bundled chi a Cat o Deer's dreamy creativity, o a Tiger o Horse's readiness to spring into action, qo gain windows into what may be going on inside — always chi the goal of correcting qa own inner deficiencies ut being gracious chi the shortcomings of others, ma excusing harm.",
    "page.about.p.everybody-else-has-their-own-four": "Everybody else has their own kaahibʼ xul too, ut it can help to know what qo're all working chi so qo can naw each other better ut enjoy qa diferencias instead of fighting over them. Different xul have different strengths ut each totem carries its own naʼlebʼ.",
    "page.about.section-label.the-system": "Sistema",
