    "article.sacredRoles.section-label.totem-astrology": "Totem Astrology",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.seeker-mage-and-royal-three-distinct": "Seeker, Mage, ut Royal — oxibʼ distinct ways every Values Triangle xul relates to its core value.",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.the-same-archetypal-structure-repeats-in": "The same archetypal structure repeats in every Values Triangle. Each triangle is a group of oxibʼ xul li includes one Seeker, one Mage, ut one Royal — oxibʼ distinct ways of relating to li Triangle's Core Value. Each xul embodies their Core Value like a banner, just preferring to access it chi their own unique perspective.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-seeker-in-every-triangle-the": "<strong>The Seeker</strong> — In every triangle the Seeker is the one who pursues, acquires, ut accumulates the Core Value, drawn to gather more of it o build it up themselves depending on their proclivities. For example, the Power ut Harmony Seekers always seem to be in hot pursuit of their Core Value, chasing after it while the Seekers of Idealism ut Security take a more active role in building their Core Value up directly, starting chi ru where they're at. The Security Seeker sets to work placing the blocks of the Pyramid one after the other, ut Idealism insists upon Freedom at every turn chi a pure passion li dares somebody to stop o even try to slow it down. They are the Drivers of each pack, ensuring li things get done ut empires get built, pushing for the team to get looked after ut making sure everyone has somewhere to rest at the end of night.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-mage-each-mage-in-their": "<strong>The Mage</strong> — Each Mage in their triangle understands their Core Value so intuitively li it becomes almost a plaything. Thus they are happy to work behind the scenes, wielding their Core Value subtly ut deploying their strength in it chi strategic intelligence. It's more of a game to them than the deadly seriousness chi which the other two Roles treat their Core Values. At times the Mages might ma even appear to be in possession of their Core Value at all, but aʼin is just a surface-level appearance - they can access it chi lightning quickness at any time. The Mages are as committed to their goals as anybody, they're just going to have a good time dancing across the boundaries ut testing the limits all along the way. Playfulness is part the package, but they've got an excellent naw of their Core Value whenever it truly counts.",
    "article.sacredRoles.li.the-royal-these-four-animals-embody": "<strong>The Royal</strong> — These kaahibʼ xul embody their Core Value at the center of their very Being, serving as Role Models of them ut wielding li Core Value chi a natural air of authority. Because of aʼin, others will follow their lead, so Spiderman rules apply: chi great power comes great responsibility! Royals often assume they have priority, ut aʼin assumption works wonders in getting them a pass straight to the front of the line ut directly to the center of the stage. The trick is in understating li it's ma just a privilege to be out here in front; it's also hard work! The poyanam are directly counting on you for direction, so li sense of knowing just what to do next better come in handy ma only for you but also for all those watching you to see how things get done. The Royals are born leaders who make the best use of the spotlight for showcasing what's important.",
    "article.sacredRoles.p.what-follows-on-the-values-triangles": "What follows on the <a href=\"totem-astrology.html\">Values Triangles</a> page is the canon for each triangle: the oxibʼ xul ut how each one lives its role as Seeker, Mage, o Royal.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.section-label.the-four-royals": "Kaahibʼ Royals",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h2.celestial-earthly-realms": "Celestial & Earthly Realms",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.of-the-twelve-totem-animals-four": "Of the kabʼlaju totem xul, kaahibʼ carry the Sacred Role of Royal — one in each Values Triangle. Together they form a double sovereignty over the zodiac: the <strong>Dragon</strong> ut <strong>Phoenix</strong> as King ut Queen of the <strong>Celestial Realm</strong>, ut the <strong>Tiger</strong> ut <strong>Bear</strong> as King ut Queen of the <strong>Earthly Realm</strong>.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h3.the-celestial-realm": "Celestial Realm",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.the-dragon-and-phoenix-reign-over": "The Dragon ut Phoenix reign over the realm of ideas ut ethereal thought structures — templates, proclamations, standards, ut the architecture of how things ought to be held in mind before they are lived in the body. The Dragon guards power ut the templates of excellence; the Phoenix proclaims security through beauty, display, ut the visible promise li all is well.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.h3.the-earthly-realm": "Earthly Realm",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.the-tiger-and-bear-reign-over": "The Tiger ut Bear reign over the realm of instincts ut juicy, sensuous experience — conviction felt in the chest, abundance tasted at the table, ideals embodied in motion, ut harmony curated in the flesh of daily life. The Tiger radiates inspiration as living proof; the Bear, as Royal of Harmony, is guardian ut protector of peace, holding the atmosphere others settle into through generosity, refuge, ut unhurried authority.",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.li.the-dragon-royal-of-power-prestige": "<strong>The Dragon</strong> — Royal of Power & Prestige (Celestial King)",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.li.the-phoenix-royal-of-stability-security": "<strong>The Phoenix</strong> — Royal of Stability & Security (Celestial Queen)",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.li.the-tiger-royal-of-inspiration-idealism": "<strong>The Tiger</strong> — Royal of Inspiration & Idealism (Earthly King)",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.li.the-bear-royal-of-peace-harmony": "<strong>The Bear</strong> — Royal of Peace & Harmony (Earthly Queen)",
    "article.sacredRoles.four-royals.p.each-royal-embodies-its-core-value": "Each Royal embodies its Core Value at the center of its being. Read how all kabʼlaju xul live their Sacred Roles on the <a href=\"totem-astrology.html\">Values Triangles</a> page.",
    "article.sacredRoles.h2.explore-the-values-triangles": "Ilok Values Triangles",
