    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.the-same-totem-animal-at-the": "The same totem xul at the same pillar — o the same xul in a different \"ring\" born 12, 24, o 36 years apart. Same guía; wonderfully different poyanam.",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.totem-connections": "<a href=\"connections.html?v=20260807\">← Totem Connections</a>",
    "page.connType.same-as-me.p.the-same-totem-animal-at-the.2": "The same totem xul at the same level — someone who shares aa Spirit, Mind, Heart, o Body guía exactly. It can also be poyanam chi ru different 'rings' so to speak — in other words poyanam born 12, 24, 36, o some other multiple of 12 years apart chi ru you. For example, I am a Fire Tiger born in 1986, but I have some wonderful Tiger junkabʼaal ut friends who are born in different Tiger rings — one of my uncles is a Water Tiger born in 1962, my son is a Metal Tiger born in 2010, ut several dear friends, students, ut companions are Earth Tigers born in 1998. I've also had coworkers who were born in the junabʼ of the Wood Tiger, 1974. It can be cool to see how aa xul act when they've got different elemental flavors charging their energy in other poyanam. It can also be neat to find poyanam born on the same exact birthdate as you, so they've got all the same xul guía, o at least 3 out of 4 if the hour xul is different, ut to see how they've chosen to play their hand differently than the way you've chosen to play yours — kind of like how 'identical' twins are different in many respects, but share lots of things in other areas. Free will is a powerful thing, ut aʼin connection shows li most clearly. The birth xul guiding them are the same, but the poyanam being guided still turn out completely ut wonderfully different :)",
